# Pinned refs for the real-collector workflow's two jobs. tests/collector/collector-gh.sh and
# tests/collector/toolkit.sh source this file (for tests/examples/regen-collector-snapshots.sh and
# tests/testbed/run-testbed-stage.sh) and tests/examples/check_utilities_pins.py reads it — it is the
# ONE place to bump.
#
# Bumping a pin is a reviewed change, exactly like a dependency bump: open a PR that changes the
# ref here AND commits the regenerated docs/examples/_expected/** in the same PR
# (see CONTRIBUTING.md -> "Regenerating the collector snapshots"), and keeps the testbed stage
# (tests/testbed/run-testbed-stage.sh) green.
#
# Refs MUST be a tag or a full commit SHA. A floating branch name (master, main, ...) is not allowed.

# AbsaOSS/living-doc-collector-gh - provides the `doc-source` and `ui-tests` mining modes, and the
# runtime requirements.txt the job builds the collector's venv from.
COLLECTOR_GH_REF=93faed7fb3afcc6514a494114ee25a1fff0fe3ea

# AbsaOSS/living-doc-toolkit - provides the `normalize-docs`, `normalize-tests` and `coverage-matrix`
# commands, and the runtime requirements.txt the job builds the toolkit's venv from.
TOOLKIT_REF=ed03f179ce6f894f51e48695827331c48a585c21
